5.2 Human-LLM Judge Alignment (RQ2)
Human-Aligned Evaluation. To demonstrate the
human-alignment of our evaluation metrics, we
validate GPT-5 mini as evaluator J against 42
region- and language-matched annotators, with
three independent ratings for 1,250 Gold-mode di-
alogues (Appendix M). As shown in Table3, J
achieves 90.1% ±1 agreement and 0.581 MAE
against human consensus, comparing favorably
to the human–human agreement baseline (87.5%,
0.727 MAE). Its slight negative bias (−0.126) fur-
ther suggests stricter-than-human scoring, reduc-
ing the risk of score inflation. Therefore, we treat
J as adequate for aggregate benchmark compar-
isons, but not as a replacement for expert adjudica-
tion of cultural truth.
Single Judge vs. Ensembles. To assess eval-
uation circularity, we compared 11 models and
165 three-judge ensembles for the role ofJ (Ap-
pendix K.2, Table 11). GPT-5 mini remains the
mosthuman-alignedmodelandiscompetitivewith
the best ensembles, supporting its use as the sole
evaluator. These ablations support GPT-5 mini as
a calibrated and practical judge for this harness.

