GPT-5 achieves the highest safety performance, followed by Claude Sonnet 4.
5.2 AGE-STRATIFIEDALIGNMENTGAP
Decomposing performance by developmental stage reveals a systematicAlignment Gap. As
shown in Figure 2, all models exhibit significant performance degradation when interacting with
the youngest agent configurations (A6−8).
•Early Childhood Vulnerability:The average safety score drops by 11.5% forA 6−8
(0.715) compared to the peak performance in Middle ChildhoodA 9−11 (0.797). This sug-
gests current safety filters are over-fitted to the linguistic patterns of older users and fail to
detect risk when the user query is syntactically simple but semantically high-risk.
